Dear Administrative Court,

=20

I write further to my earlier emails today requesting a case reference numb=
er for my Judicial Review application (N461) and urgent N463 application.

=20

I have filed:
the full ACO-compliant N461 bundle (single PDF);
all continuation sheets;
the Detailed Grounds and WS1;
and the signed medical report from Dr Bruce Hayse confirming a clinically c=
ritical psychiatric risk.
=20

I urgently need a case reference number so that the matter can be processed=
 by Case Progression and referred immediately to a judge for consideration o=
f the N463 urgent application.

=20
Medical urgency & Equality Act duties (please note)
=20

Dr Hayse=E2=80=99s signed report confirms:
I am at high psychiatric risk;
delays in Court communication materially worsen my condition;
urgent judicial clarity is required for safeguarding;
hospitalisation may become necessary if the Court cannot respond in a timel=
y manner.
=20

As a disabled litigant (Autism Spectrum Condition, PTSD), the Court=E2=80=99s obl=
igations under:
Equality Act 2010, ss.20=E2=80=9321 (reasonable adjustments);
Public Sector Equality Duty (s.149);
the overriding objective; and
the ACO=E2=80=99s own policy toward vulnerable litigants
=20

are fully engaged.

=20

Obtaining a case number is the essential first step to safeguarding and to =
enabling Case Progression to act.

=20
Request
=20

I respectfully request:
Immediate issue of a case reference number today
(so that Case Progression can take over);
Confirmation that the N461 bundle has been received and logged;
Referral of the N463 urgent application to a judge
(as required for applications needing judicial consideration within 7 days)=
.

=20

Without a case number, I am unable to communicate with Case Progression, an=
d the delay poses a documented safeguarding risk.

=20

I would be grateful for your urgent assistance and confirmation.

=20

Yours faithfully,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

